    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shattered_spire_note_1">Charred stone and melted glass for a hundred metres in every direction. The pillar that stood here did not fall — it was torn apart.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shattered_spire_note_2">A torn page from an adept\'s journal: \'The Great Work exceeds all projections. Wisdom can wait. We must press on.\'</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shattered_spire_note_3">Hermetic diagrams etched into the surviving stones — a circle of protection, poorly squared, clearly overstressed.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shattered_spire_note_4">A passage has been blasted open downward. Automatons still move in the dark below, following old instructions.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shattered_spire_note_5">The passage descends into intact chambers beneath the rubble. The Ruins of the Hermetic School still function, after a fashion.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_abyssal_lagoon_note_1">Like ignorance itself, the water here has no bottom. Strange lights pulse from impossible depths.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_abyssal_lagoon_note_2">Fish pulled from the deep glow faintly and dissolve within minutes. What fed on them?</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_abyssal_lagoon_note_3">A torn map marks this lagoon with a single word: \'DO NOT FISH.\' The hand that wrote it was trembling.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_abyssal_lagoon_note_4">Something rises to the surface and sinks again. Massive. Ancient. Curious.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_abyssal_lagoon_note_5">The dark water parts. The Abyssal Ruins loom below — vast, alien, and older than any temple raised by human hands.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_sunken_grotto_note_1">Two stone pillars rise from the grotto floor like a drowned echo of Jakin and Boaz, carved with script no living scholar can read.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_sunken_grotto_note_2">The fish scatter without warning — something large passes below.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_sunken_grotto_note_3">A waterlogged journal drifts by: \'The temple they found beneath the water was not abandoned. It was waiting.\'</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_sunken_grotto_note_4">A submerged archway pulses with faint ancient light, its keystone still in place. The current pulls toward it.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_sunken_grotto_note_5">The archway is clear. The Drowned Temple lies beyond — something old keeps watch within.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_dwarven_depths_note_1">Ancient walls carved with masons\' marks pulse faintly. The operative masons who cut this place are long gone.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_dwarven_depths_note_2">A colossal forge stands at the passage end, its fires somehow still burning after centuries — fires that once cast bronze for the Temple.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_dwarven_depths_note_3">Iron golems stand dormant in the alcoves. Their eyes flicker as you quarry nearby.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_dwarven_depths_note_4">The marks around the forge are a warning — something was bound here, and it grows restless.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_dwarven_depths_note_5">The golems rise fully to life. Hiram\'s Forge awakens — its guardians await those brave enough to enter.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_corrupted_canopy_note_1">The trees here bleed shadow where cut. The wood writhes and resists the axe.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_corrupted_canopy_note_2">A shadow beast watches from the canopy. It does not attack — it only observes.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_corrupted_canopy_note_3">Old sanctum stones show through the twisted trunks, their sacred marks scratched out. Something still lives there.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_corrupted_canopy_note_4">The corruption spreads as you work. The canopy hungers for the light it has lost.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_corrupted_canopy_note_5">The canopy parts. The Defiled Sanctum rises from the shadow-wood — its doors open, waiting.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_whispering_grove_note_1">The acacias here whisper in a language older than any known tongue. Some say they remember where the Master was laid.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_whispering_grove_note_2">Stone foundations visible beneath the roots — the remains of a lodge built long before the forest.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_whispering_grove_note_3">A hermit\'s warning carved in bark: \'The clearing at the grove\'s heart is not what it was. Stay away.\'</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_whispering_grove_note_4">Corrupted vines reach toward you as you chop. The grove resists your presence.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_whispering_grove_note_5">A gap in the canopy reveals ruins at the grove\'s heart. The Ruins of the Cedar Forest call to be explored.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_thieves_den_note_1">A crumpled ledger page: names, dates, and sums. Someone has been tracking bribes paid to a figure called the Warden.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_thieves_den_note_2">Scratched into the wall: \'For those who prove themselves — the Sanctum awaits. No oath, no questions.\'</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_thieves_den_note_3">A torn letter warning a member to stay away from the eastern tunnels. No reason is given.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_thieves_den_note_4">A wax-sealed map fragment. The seal is a crude forgery of a square and compasses, set crooked.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_thieves_den_note_5">The last passage opens into a vaulted chamber. At the far end, a reinforced door bears the same false seal. The Sanctum of False Brothers lies beyond.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_crumbling_watchtower_note_1">Fresh rope marks on the windowsills. Someone climbs this tower of confused tongues regularly.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_crumbling_watchtower_note_2">A hidden cache inside a cracked wall: lockpicks, a short blade, and a coded ledger.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_crumbling_watchtower_note_3">The ledger is a tally of stolen goods and split payments. The ruffians operate out of somewhere beneath the hill.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_crumbling_watchtower_note_4">A trapdoor in the floor, recently oiled, its hinges silent. Worn boot prints surround it.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_crumbling_watchtower_note_5">The trapdoor opens onto a carved stairway going deep into the earth. The Den of Shadows waits below.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_copper_caverns_note_1">Scratches mark the gallery walls, too deep and wide for any pick.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_copper_caverns_note_2">Old quarrying tools, twisted and bent. Whatever was here left in a hurry.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_copper_caverns_note_3">A quarryman\'s torn note: \'We broke through to something below. The overseer sealed the lower shaft. He won\'t say why.\'</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_copper_caverns_note_4">Tremors from below. Dust falls from the ceiling in slow waves. Something stirs.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_copper_caverns_note_5">The sealed shaft gives way. A vast cavern opens beneath — the Collapsed Quarry lies ahead.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shadow_vault_note_1">A dossier on every Master Builder in the City. Someone has been watching the workshops for years.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shadow_vault_note_2">A vault door, partially ajar. Inside — crates of stolen tools, aprons, and sealed scroll cases.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shadow_vault_note_3">One scroll case is different from the others. It bears the seal of the Temple works. It is empty.</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shadow_vault_note_4">A private journal: \'The Conspiracy does not seek the Light. It seeks the Master\'s Word — taken by force, never earned.\'</string>
    <string name="skilling_dungeon_shadow_vault_note_5">The deepest vault is not locked. It is guarded. What waits inside is the Conspiracy\'s darkest secret — and its most dangerous protectors.</string>
